+# nta-signer
+
+Reference XBT-NTA signer for TIDES payees that are **not** DATUM gateways (SOV-017), such as
+xbt-agentpay pay-with-work providers. Gateways keep signing themselves (`nta_key_file`, the
+`0x4e` message). Nothing here is deployed; it is rnd-only while the freeze holds.
+
+Under NTA every coinbase payee `OP_1 <K>` needs K's BIP340 signature over
+`TaggedHash("XBT-NTA/attestation", ser(script) || height || nBits || hashPrevBlock)` for the block
+being built. This daemon follows the tip of any node it can reach over RPC, signs each new tip for
+every key it holds, and posts the signature to Prime. A payee whose signature for a tip is
+missing is **carried** (its share waits in TIDES carry), never lost; it is paid again once it signs.
+
+```sh
+nta-signer run --rpc http://127.0.0.1:8332 --rpc-cookie ~/.bitcoin/.cookie \
+  --key-file ~/.config/nta/provider.key \
+  --prime https://pool.example/api/nta/attest        # or primed's loopback http://127.0.0.1:28916/nta/attest
+nta-signer pubkey --key-file ~/.config/nta/provider.key   # K and the payee script, never the secret
+```
+
+- **Tip.** `waitfornewblock` long-poll (falls back to polling `--poll-ms`), then
+  `getblockchaininfo` + `getmininginfo.next.bits` (v29+), else `getblocktemplate`, else on regtest
+  the tip's own bits. Signing takes ~25 µs; the rest is how fast your node hears of the block.
+- **Posting.** One POST per key per Prime per tip; one retry on `409` (Prime's node had not seen the
+  tip yet). Prime allows `nta-attest-per-tip` (default 2) per script per tip, so do not run two
+  signers for one key against one Prime. Unreachable Prime: retried every second for 30 s while the
+  tip holds. A newer tip supersedes all pending posts.
+- **Keys.** 64 hex characters, mode 600; refused if group- or world-readable; never logged.
+  `--token-file` (mode 600) if Prime sets `nta-attest-token-file`.
+
+## Which secret: BIP86 wallets
+
+NTA pays `OP_1 <K>` and checks K's signature directly, so the key file must hold the secret of the
+**output** key K, not the wallet's internal key. For a BIP86 (key-path only) address:
+
+- internal key `P = d·G` (negate d if P has odd y),
+- tweak `t = TaggedHash("TapTweak", x(P))`,
+- output key `K = P + t·G`, whose secret is **`d + t` (mod n)**.
+
+`nta-signer bip86-tweak --internal-key-file d.hex --out k.hex` does exactly that (checked against the
+BIP341 `keyPathSpending` vectors) and writes the result mode 600. Get `d` from your wallet's
+descriptor export (`listdescriptors true`, derive the child for your address). The output secret
+spends the address too: guard it like the wallet itself, and prefer a dedicated payout address
+for the hot signer.
+
+## Prime side
+
+`POST /nta/attest` on primed's stats listener (loopback), or `POST /api/nta/attest` on the pool site,
+which forwards there with a per-IP limit. Body:
+`{"version":1,"key":hex32,"height":n,"nbits":"207fffff","prev":<display hex>,"sig":hex64}`.
+Answers: `200 accepted|duplicate`, `400` bad body, `403` token / not a live TIDES payee in the
+window, `409` not Prime's node's tip (`tip` says which is), `422` wrong height/bits or bad signature,
+`429` per-script-per-tip or global limit, `503` NTA off.
